cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "datasource-duckdb: Lean 4 bindings to DuckDB for Parquet and CSV"
abstract: >
  A data source implements a repository, and this one gets facts out of files that
  were not built to be queried. It is a small Lean 4 FFI over DuckDB for loading
  Parquet, CSV and JSON into Lean, so a sim-first dataset can be read by the same
  language that states the properties it has to satisfy.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/datasource-duckdb"
keywords:
  - lean4
  - duckdb
  - parquet
  - ffi

# DuckDB is linked, not vendored: it is a system library here, so what this repository
# holds is the binding and not the database.
references:

  - type: software
    title: "DuckDB: an in-process SQL OLAP database management system"
    authors:
      - family-names: Raasveldt
        given-names: Mark
      - family-names: Mühleisen
        given-names: Hannes
    url: "https://duckdb.org/"
    notes: >
      The engine every call in this repository reaches. Linked as a system library rather
      than vendored, so its version is the machine's and this repository does not pin it.

  - type: software
    title: "Lean 4: a theorem prover and programming language"
    authors:
      - name: "The Lean FRO"
    url: "https://leanprover.github.io/"
    notes: "The language the bindings are written in and the reason they exist."
